<title>USA: Federal-Mogul Corp to name new CEO - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Federal-Mogul Corp to name new CEO - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal-Mogul Corp is expected to appoint Richard Snell as its chairman and chief executive officer on Monday, the Wall Street Journal reported.</p>
<p>The newspaper said in its Monday edition that Snell would also become the company's president, citing people close to the automotive supplier.</p>
<p>Snell was president and chief executive officer of Tenneco Inc unit Tenneco Automotive, it said.</p>
<p>The newspaper said he would replace Dennis Gormley, who resigned in September.</p>
</text>
